---
// Post-event survey callout — first on-site link to the live /survey-2026
// page (previously reachable only via blast links). ?src=site feeds the
// survey's `source` column so site-driven responses stay separable from
// the sms/email blasts.
//
// Navy section for contrast against the cream hero above and cream
// waitlist below — navy was the lineup section's color on the live site,
// so it reads as the same design system.
---

<section id="survey" class="relative bg-bp-navy text-paper px-5 md:px-10 py-24 md:py-32">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center" data-reveal>
    <h2
      class="block-print font-[var(--font-display)] uppercase font-black leading-[0.85] text-[clamp(2.5rem,8vw,6rem)] mb-6"
      data-ink="cream"
      data-ghost
      style="--ghost: var(--color-bp-cyan);"
    >
      How Was the Block?
    </h2>
    <p class="text-base md:text-lg opacity-90 max-w-xl mx-auto mb-10">
      Tell us what you liked, what you didn't, and who you want on the block
      next year. It takes about two minutes, and we read every one.
    </p>
    <a
      href="/survey-2026?src=site"
      class="group inline-flex items-center gap-3 bg-bp-pink text-paper px-8 py-4 text-sm md:text-base uppercase tracking-[0.25em] font-bold"
      style="filter: url(#ink-bleed-soft); box-shadow: -4px 4px 0 var(--color-bp-cyan);"
    >
      Take the Survey
      <span aria-hidden="true" class="transition-transform group-hover:translate-x-1">→</span>
    </a>
  </div>
</section>
